VCycene Internship – Mechanical Design & Product Development

This repository documents the work completed during my internship at VCycene, where I focused on the mechanical design, prototyping, and fabrication of a product used to help the company demonstrate and market its technology.
My role centred on taking a concept from early sketches to a functional, test-ready prototype through iterative design and hands-on building.

Ended up making a plant pot which followed the design of VCycene's composter

During my internship at VCycene, I was responsible for designing and developing a mechanical prototype that would serve as a customer-facing demo unit. The goal was to create a reliable, visually clear, and easy-to-use product that effectively showcased the company’s capabilities.

My work included:
- Gathering mechanical and functional requirements
- Developing multiple design concepts
- CAD modelling and mechanical assembly creation
- Designing motion, support, and structural elements
- Prototyping using machining, 3D printing, and hand-building
- Testing structural performance, fit, and usability
- Iterating based on developing constraints and objectives

This repository contains design files and documentation from my work.

This internship strengthened several core engineering skills:
- How to take a mechanical idea from sketch → CAD → prototype → refined system
- Making design decisions that balance performance, manufacturability, and cost
- Working within tight timelines typical of a startup environment
- Communicating engineering reasoning with team leads and other designers
- Building reliable hardware through repeated iteration and testing

